{"title": "Quant Super Practice — Mock #148", "duration_min": 20.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>Two numbers are in the ratio of 9: 11. If 7 is added to the smaller number and 8 is added to the larger number, then the ratio becomes 5: 6. What would be the ratio when 12 is subtracted from a smaller number and 6 is subtracted from a larger number?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 9:11 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 7 &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 8 &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 5:6 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2332;&#2348; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 12 &#2328;&#2335;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 6 &#2328;&#2335;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["3: 8", "4: 7", "1: 2", "2: 3"], "options_hi": ["3: 8", "4: 7", "1: 2", "2: 3"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the smaller number = 9x and the larger number = 11x</p><p>ATQ,</p><p>(9x + 7)/(11x + 8) = 5/6</p><p>54x + 42 = 55x + 40</p><p>X = 2</p><p>Smaller number = 18 and larger number = 22</p><p>Required ratio = (18  -  12): (22  -  6) = 6: 16 = 3: 8</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the smaller number = 9x and the larger number = 11x</p><p>ATQ,</p><p>(9x + 7)/(11x + 8) = 5/6</p><p>54x + 42 = 55x + 40</p><p>X = 2</p><p>Smaller number = 18 and larger number = 22</p><p>Required ratio = (18  -  12): (22  -  6) = 6: 16 = 3: 8</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the mean proportional between 100 and 225.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>100 &#2324;&#2352; 225 &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2350;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["450", "350", "150", "250"], "options_hi": ["450", "350", "150", "250"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Mean proportion = &#8730;(100 * 225)</p><p>= 10 * 15</p><p>= 150</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Mean proportion = &#8730;(100 * 225)</p><p>= 10 * 15</p><p>= 150</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>If 12: 18 :: p: 48 and (p  -  12): (p  -  2) :: (q + 6): (q + 27), then what is the value of 'q'?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 12: 18 :: p: 48 &#2324;&#2352; (p - 12): (p - 2) :: (q + 6): (q + 27) &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; 'q' &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["30", "32", "34", "36"], "options_hi": ["30", "32", "34", "36"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>According to the question:</p><p>12: 18 :: p: 48</p><p>12 * 48 = p * 18</p><p>p = 32</p><p>Now, (p  -  12): (p  -  2) :: (q + 6): (q + 27)</p><p>(32  -  12): (32  -  2) :: (q + 6): (q + 27)</p><p>20 * (q + 27) = (q + 6) * 30</p><p><b>q = 36</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>According to the question:</p><p>12: 18 :: p: 48</p><p>12 * 48 = p * 18</p><p>p = 32</p><p>Now, (p  -  12): (p  -  2) :: (q + 6): (q + 27)</p><p>(32  -  12): (32  -  2) :: (q + 6): (q + 27)</p><p>20 * (q + 27) = (q + 6) * 30</p><p><b>q = 36</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>If third proportion of 64 and 72 is x and mean proportion of (x + 19) and (7 + 2x) is y, then what is the value of (x + y)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 64 &#2324;&#2352; 72 &#2325;&#2366; &#2340;&#2371;&#2340;&#2368;&#2351;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; x &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; (x + 19) &#2324;&#2352; (7 + 2x) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; y &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; (x + y) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["203", "211", "245", "206"], "options_hi": ["203", "211", "245", "206"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Given, third proportion of 64 and 72 is x</p><p>=&gt; x = (72 * 72)/64</p><p>=&gt; x = 81</p><p>And mean proportion of (x + 19) and (7 + 2x) is y</p><p>=&gt; y = &radic;[(81 + 19)(7 + 2 * 81)]</p><p>=&gt; y = &radic;(100 * 169)</p><p>=&gt; y = 10 * 13</p><p>=&gt; y = 130</p><p>Hence, (x + y) = 81 + 130 = 211</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Given, third proportion of 64 and 72 is x</p><p>=&gt; x = (72 * 72)/64</p><p>=&gt; x = 81</p><p>And mean proportion of (x + 19) and (7 + 2x) is y</p><p>=&gt; y = &radic;[(81 + 19)(7 + 2 * 81)]</p><p>=&gt; y = &radic;(100 * 169)</p><p>=&gt; y = 10 * 13</p><p>=&gt; y = 130</p><p>Hence, (x + y) = 81 + 130 = 211</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A is chasing B in the same interval of time. A Jumps 8 times, while B Jumps 6 times. But the distance covered by A in 7 jumps is the same as that of B in 5 jumps. The ratio between the speeds of A and B is.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;&#2366;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; B &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2368;&#2331;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2352;&#2361;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; A 8 &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2331;&#2354;&#2366;&#2305;&#2327; &#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; B 6 &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2331;&#2354;&#2366;&#2305;&#2327; &#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2354;&#2375;&#2325;&#2367;&#2344; A &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; 7 &#2331;&#2354;&#2366;&#2305;&#2327;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368;, B &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; 5 &#2331;&#2354;&#2366;&#2305;&#2327;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;-</p>", "options_en": ["32 : 24", "30 : 56", "20 : 21", "28 : 36"], "options_hi": ["32 : 24", "30 : 56", "20 : 21", "28 : 36"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>7 jumps of A = 5 jumps of B</p><p>A = <img width=23 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21005/image056.png\"></p><p>8 jumps of A =<img width=32 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21005/image057.png\"></p><p>Ratio between the speeds of A and B = <img width=72 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21005/image058.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>7 jumps of A = 5 jumps of B</p><p>A = <img width=23 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21005/image056.png\"></p><p>8 jumps of A =<img width=32 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21005/image057.png\"></p><p>Ratio between the speeds of A and B = <img width=72 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21005/image058.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>The population of villages A and B is in the ratio of 9:7 respectively and ratio of man, woman and children in each village is 4:1:5 respectively. If the population of village A is 7560, then population of children in village B is -</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2327;&#2366;&#2305;&#2357; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2344;&#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 9: 7 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2327;&#2366;&#2305;&#2357; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306;, &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306;, &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 4: 1: 5 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2327;&#2366;&#2306;&#2357; A &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2344;&#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 7560 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2327;&#2366;&#2306;&#2357; B &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2344;&#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["3260", "2940", "3140", "2570"], "options_hi": ["3260", "2940", "3140", "2570"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Population of village A = 7560</p><p>Population of village B = 7560 * 7/9 = 5880</p><p>Population of children in village B = 5880 * 5/10 = 2940</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Population of village A = 7560</p><p>Population of village B = 7560 * 7/9 = 5880</p><p>Population of children in village B = 5880 * 5/10 = 2940</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>If P &#8758; Q = 15 &#8758; 16 and Q &#8758; R = 16 &#8758; 17, then (P + Q) &#8758; (Q + R) &#8758; (R + P) is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; P &#8758; Q = 15 &#8758; 16 &#2324;&#2352; Q &#8758; R = 16 &#8758; 17 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; (P + Q) &#8758; (Q + R) &#8758; (R + P) &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;:</p>", "options_en": ["33: 31: 32", "31: 32: 33", "31: 33: 32", "32: 31: 33"], "options_hi": ["33: 31: 32", "31: 32: 33", "31: 33: 32", "32: 31: 33"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Given P: Q = 15: 16, Q: R = 16: 17</p><p>So, P: Q: R = 15: 16: 17</p><p>Now,</p><p>(P + Q) &#8758; (Q + R) &#8758; (R + P)</p><p>= (15 + 16): (16 + 17): (17 + 15)</p><p>= 31: 33: 32</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Given P: Q = 15: 16, Q: R = 16: 17</p><p>So, P: Q: R = 15: 16: 17</p><p>Now,</p><p>(P + Q) &#8758; (Q + R) &#8758; (R + P)</p><p>= (15 + 16): (16 + 17): (17 + 15)</p><p>= 31: 33: 32</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>In a forest, tigers and parrots are in the ratio 7: 5 respectively and together they have 60 heads. Find the number of legs of tigers and parrots together in the forest.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2332;&#2306;&#2327;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2348;&#2366;&#2328; &#2324;&#2352; &#2340;&#2379;&#2340;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 7:5 &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; 60 &#2360;&#2367;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2332;&#2306;&#2327;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2366;&#2328; &#2324;&#2352; &#2340;&#2379;&#2340;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2376;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["170", "190", "180", "200"], "options_hi": ["170", "190", "180", "200"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>We know, each tiger has 1 head and 4 legs while each parrot has 1 head and 2 legs.</p><p>Let there are 7a tigers and 5a parrots in the forest. Then,</p><p>7a + 5a = 60</p><p>12a = 60</p><p>a = 5</p><p>Therefore, number of legs of tigers and parrots together in the forest = 4 * 7a + 2 * 5a</p><p>= 38a</p><p>= 38 * 5</p><p>= <b>190</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>We know, each tiger has 1 head and 4 legs while each parrot has 1 head and 2 legs.</p><p>Let there are 7a tigers and 5a parrots in the forest. Then,</p><p>7a + 5a = 60</p><p>12a = 60</p><p>a = 5</p><p>Therefore, number of legs of tigers and parrots together in the forest = 4 * 7a + 2 * 5a</p><p>= 38a</p><p>= 38 * 5</p><p>= <b>190</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Mean proportional of M and N is 30. If fourth proportional of 12, 18 and 40 is M, then N = __.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>M &#2324;&#2352; N &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; 30 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 12, 18 &#2324;&#2352; 40 &#2325;&#2366; &#2330;&#2380;&#2341;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; M &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; N = __ &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["25", "20", "15", "45"], "options_hi": ["25", "20", "15", "45"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Fourth proportional of 12, 18 and 40 is M. So, </p><p>12: 18 :: 40: M</p><p>M = 40 * 18/12</p><p>M = 60</p><p>Now, mean proportional M and N is 30. So, </p><p>30 = &radic;(M * N)</p><p>900 = (60 * N)</p><p><b>N = 15</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Fourth proportional of 12, 18 and 40 is M. So, </p><p>12: 18 :: 40: M</p><p>M = 40 * 18/12</p><p>M = 60</p><p>Now, mean proportional M and N is 30. So, </p><p>30 = &radic;(M * N)</p><p>900 = (60 * N)</p><p><b>N = 15</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>There are three numbers P, Q, and R such that P: 2Q = 2Q: R. If P = 45 and R = 60, then find the value of Q.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; P, Q &#2324;&#2352; R &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367; P: 2Q = 2Q: R &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; P = 45 &#2324;&#2352; R = 60 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; Q &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["15", "15&radic;3", "5&radic;3", "20"], "options_hi": ["15", "15&radic;3", "5&radic;3", "20"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>P/2Q = 2Q/R</p><p>4Q<sup>2</sup> = P x R</p><p>Q<sup>2</sup> = 45 x 60/4</p><p>Q<sup>2</sup> = 45 x 15</p><p>Q = 15&radic;3</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>P/2Q = 2Q/R</p><p>4Q<sup>2</sup> = P x R</p><p>Q<sup>2</sup> = 45 x 60/4</p><p>Q<sup>2</sup> = 45 x 15</p><p>Q = 15&radic;3</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>The ratio of a number B to a number C is 1: 7. If a number A is 25% more than B, then find (A + C): B.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; B &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; C &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 1: 7 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; A, B &#2360;&#2375; 25% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; (A + C): B &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["33: 4", "33: 5", "31: 3", "28: 3"], "options_hi": ["33: 4", "33: 5", "31: 3", "28: 3"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let B = X an C = 7X</p><p>Then A = 125/100 of B</p><p>A = 5X/4</p><p>A + C = (5X/4) + 7X = 33X/4</p><p>Required ratio = (A + C): B = (33X/4): X = 33: 4</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let B = X an C = 7X</p><p>Then A = 125/100 of B</p><p>A = 5X/4</p><p>A + C = (5X/4) + 7X = 33X/4</p><p>Required ratio = (A + C): B = (33X/4): X = 33: 4</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>The ratio of number of students in section A to section B is 9: 11. Section B has 28 more students than section A. Find the total number of students in both sections.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2349;&#2366;&#2327; A &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2349;&#2366;&#2327; B &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 9:11 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2349;&#2366;&#2327; B &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2349;&#2366;&#2327; A &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2369;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 28 &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2349;&#2366;&#2327;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["320", "240", "300", "280"], "options_hi": ["320", "240", "300", "280"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let number of students in section A and section B be 9X and 11X respectively.</p><p>Given,</p><p>11X  -  9X = 28</p><p>X = 14</p><p>Total number of students = 9X + 11X = 20X = 20 * 14 = 280</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let number of students in section A and section B be 9X and 11X respectively.</p><p>Given,</p><p>11X  -  9X = 28</p><p>X = 14</p><p>Total number of students = 9X + 11X = 20X = 20 * 14 = 280</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>If a: b: c = 1/12: 1/16: 1/9, then what is the value of (a + 2b)/(2b  -  c)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; a: b: c = 1/12: 1/16: 1/9 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; (a + 2b)/(2b - c) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["15", "30", "12", "32"], "options_hi": ["15", "30", "12", "32"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>a: b: c = 1/12: 1/16: 1/9 = 12: 9: 16</p><p>Let a = 12x, b = 9x, and c = 16x</p><p>Hence, (a + 2b)/(2b  -  c) = (12x + 18x)/(18x  -  16x) = 30x/2x = 15</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>a: b: c = 1/12: 1/16: 1/9 = 12: 9: 16</p><p>Let a = 12x, b = 9x, and c = 16x</p><p>Hence, (a + 2b)/(2b  -  c) = (12x + 18x)/(18x  -  16x) = 30x/2x = 15</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>If 2A : 8 &#8759; X : (A/3), then X = ?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 2A : 8 &#8759; X : (A/3) &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; X = ?</p>", "options_en": ["A/6", "2A/3", "A<sup>2</sup>/3", "A<sup>2</sup>/12"], "options_hi": ["A/6", "2A/3", "A<sup>2</sup>/3", "A<sup>2</sup>/12"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>According to the question,</p><p>2A * (A/3) =8 * X</p><p>X = (2A<sup>2</sup>/3) * 1/8</p><p>X = A<sup>2</sup>/12</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>According to the question,</p><p>2A * (A/3) =8 * X</p><p>X = (2A<sup>2</sup>/3) * 1/8</p><p>X = A<sup>2</sup>/12</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>The fourth proportional of 2X, (X + 4), and 60 is 72.5. Find the value of X. (rounded off to one decimal)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>2X, (X + 4) &#2324;&#2352; 60 &#2325;&#2366; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; 72.5 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; X &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; (&#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2340;&#2325; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340;)&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["2.1", "2.8", "2.4", "2.6"], "options_hi": ["2.1", "2.8", "2.4", "2.6"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>ATQ,</p><p>60 * (X + 4)/2X = 72.5</p><p>60X + 240 = 145X</p><p>85X = 240</p><p>X = 2.8.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>ATQ,</p><p>60 * (X + 4)/2X = 72.5</p><p>60X + 240 = 145X</p><p>85X = 240</p><p>X = 2.8.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Which of the following ratios is the lowest?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["8: 10", "12: 15", "4: 7", "7: 9"], "options_hi": ["8: 10", "12: 15", "4: 7", "7: 9"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>8: 10 = 8/10 = 0.8</p><p>12: 15 = 4/5 = 0.8</p><p>4: 7 = 4/7 = 0.57</p><p>7: 9 = 7/9 = 0.77</p><p>Hence, 4: 7 is the lowest ratio.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>8: 10 = 8/10 = 0.8</p><p>12: 15 = 4/5 = 0.8</p><p>4: 7 = 4/7 = 0.57</p><p>7: 9 = 7/9 = 0.77</p><p>Hence, 4: 7 is the lowest ratio.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>If A: B = 7: 3, then (3B - A ): (5B  -  2A) =?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; A: B = 7: 3 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; (3B - A ): (5B - 2A) =?</p>", "options_en": ["2: 1", "4: 3", "21: 29", "3: 4"], "options_hi": ["2: 1", "4: 3", "21: 29", "3: 4"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let A = 7k and B = 3k</p><p>Now, (3B -  A): (5B  -  2A) = (9k  -  7k): (15k  -  14k) = 2: 1</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let A = 7k and B = 3k</p><p>Now, (3B -  A): (5B  -  2A) = (9k  -  7k): (15k  -  14k) = 2: 1</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>One-third of a number and twice of another number are in the ratio of 1:4 respectively. What is the ratio of the numbers?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; 1/3 &#2324;&#2352; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 1:4 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["2:5", "1:3", "3:2", "4:1"], "options_hi": ["2:5", "1:3", "3:2", "4:1"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let numbers are x and y.</p><p>(x/3):2y = 1:4</p><p>x:y = 6:4 = 3:2</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let numbers are x and y.</p><p>(x/3):2y = 1:4</p><p>x:y = 6:4 = 3:2</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>The number x and y are respectively 45% and 30% more than third number z. find y : x.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; x &#2324;&#2352; y &#2340;&#2368;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; z &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 45% &#2324;&#2352; 30% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; y : x &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["13 : 14", "26 : 29", "27 : 29", "13 : 15"], "options_hi": ["13 : 14", "26 : 29", "27 : 29", "13 : 15"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the third number(z) = 100</p><p>x = 100 * 145/100 = 145</p><p>y = 100 * 130/100 = 130</p><p>y : x = 130 : 145 = 26 : 29</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the third number(z) = 100</p><p>x = 100 * 145/100 = 145</p><p>y = 100 * 130/100 = 130</p><p>y : x = 130 : 145 = 26 : 29</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>A, B and C invest in the ratio of 1/3 : 1/5 : 1/6. Find the amount of profit received by B out of total profit of Rs. 2562.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A, B &#2324;&#2352; C 1/3: 1/5: 1/6 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; 2562 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; B &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349;&#2366;&#2306;&#2358; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 690", "Rs. 700", "Rs. 732", "Rs. 740"], "options_hi": ["690 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "700 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "732 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "740 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Ratio in which A, B and C received the profit amount = 1/3 : 1/5 : 1/6</p><p>=&gt; 10/30 : 6/30 : 5/30 or 10 : 6 : 5</p><p>Amount of profit received by B = 6/21 * 2562 = Rs. 732</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Ratio in which A, B and C received the profit amount = 1/3 : 1/5 : 1/6</p><p>=&gt; 10/30 : 6/30 : 5/30 or 10 : 6 : 5</p><p>Amount of profit received by B = 6/21 * 2562 = Rs. 732</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}]}